  "targetText": "7. Prove uniqueness for every positive same-square macro alternativeFor ANY positive G with G²=I_H_P−A², pull it back by e⁻¹. Its positivity and square are preserved, so the shared real scalar uniqueness theorem forces e⁻¹Ge=Γ. Conjugate back to obtain G=Γ_P. The universal alternative-root quantifier is outside the every-f energy conjunction and assumes no alternative energy identity.G≥0, G2=IHP−A2 ⟹ e−1Ge=Γ ⟹ G=ΓP.Corresponding Lean step  have hUnique (G : HP →L[ℝ] HP) (hG : G.IsPositive)\n      (hGSq : G*G=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A) : G=ΓP := by\n    let G0 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν := e.symm.conjStarAlgEquiv G\n    have hG0 : G0.IsPositive := by\n      simpa only [G0,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply,e.symm.adjoint_eq_symm] using\n        hG.conj_adjoint (e.symm : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)\n   ",
